        note: 'Announced 9 March 2022 alongside a $10bn buyback authorisation, the 20-for-1 split took effect 6 June 2022 — shareholders received 19 additional shares for every 1 held. Pre-split the stock traded around $2,700–$2,800; post-split roughly $120–$140. The stated purpose was accessibility for retail investors, flexibility in employee equity comp, and a signal of confidence. This was Amazon’s fourth split ever (the prior three were late-1990s dot-com era) and there have been none since as of early 2026. The jump from 515M to 10,189M shares between 2021 and 2022 in this series is that split, not issuance.'
